# The Quota slice: the community model (design/quota/04-SYSTEMS.md, game/engine/world/community.mjs) and the
# granary door's fight. The gameplay engineer's file: the scenes are the story lead's (q_*.lwd); their nodes
# carry the record() and shift() lines that feed this model.
# Per street: owed (grain owed over the true yield, for a village row), notices (how thickly the notices are
# posted there), mixed (1 where Tarn and Hesh households live side by side: rhetoric bites slower), pub (1 where the
# Crown is heard), pews (how many go to the Furrow Church: q_discourse.lwd). Per
# household: bowls (one per member at the table), portion (what is in each bowl, 1 full), taken (1 when one
# of them is held). Globals: export (the train ran), blacklist, volume.notices (the carrier's volume).
# Who is missing at the Haldane table: the household's food after the requisition (H1: a child goes when it
# falls below 0.15), with Tomas held as the override (H3, from q.tomas_held; H2 when the patrols come).

@street square
name: Exchange Square
peoples: tarn, hesh
owed: 0
mixed: 1
pub: 1
pews: 1
notices: 0.6
food: 0.45
price: 1.0
wage: 1.1
work: 0.5
hunger: 0.25
theft: 0.1
school: 0.7
standing: hesh -0.1, tarn 0.3
protection: hesh 0.6, tarn 0.8
trust: police 0.5, council 0.45

@street mill
name: Mill Street
peoples: tarn, hesh
owed: 0
mixed: 1
pub: 1
pews: 1
notices: 0.8
food: 0.4
price: 1.0
wage: 0.95
work: 0.45
hunger: 0.3
theft: 0.12
school: 0.6
standing: hesh 0, tarn 0.2
protection: hesh 0.6, tarn 0.7
trust: police 0.45, council 0.4

@street haldane_yard
name: Haldane Yard
peoples: hesh
village: 1
owed: 0
mixed: 0
pub: 0
pews: 0.3
notices: 1
food: 0.35
price: 1.0
wage: 0.8
work: 0.4
hunger: 0.35
theft: 0.18
school: 0.55
standing: hesh -0.2
protection: hesh 0.5
trust: police 0.35, council 0.3

# the next village over: a village row (era 2 adds the villages one row each); the replacement inspector's
# figure lands here when Ned is blacklisted for the honest one
@street hollow
name: Tarn Hollow
peoples: tarn, hesh
village: 1
owed: 0
mixed: 1
pub: 0
pews: 0.8
notices: 0.7
food: 0.4
price: 1.0
wage: 0.85
work: 0.4
hunger: 0.3
theft: 0.12
school: 0.6
standing: hesh -0.1, tarn 0.2
protection: hesh 0.6, tarn 0.7
trust: police 0.4, council 0.35

@household haldane
name: The Haldanes
street: haldane_yard
people: hesh
hesh: 1
place: q_haldane
members: Tomas, Aaron, Anni, Ilo, Bet
taken: 0
portion: 1

@household furrowe
name: The Furrowes
street: square
people: tarn
hesh: 0
place: q_furrowe_kitchen
members: Ned, Mary, Pell, Abel
taken: 0
portion: 1

@household brack
name: The Bracks
street: mill
people: tarn
hesh: 0
place: q_brack_kitchen
members: Will, Edie, Davey
# Rose, six, eats from Edie's bowl on her knee (q_coda.lwd): in the household, not a bowl of her own
lap: Rose
taken: 0
portion: 1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the two lenses (world/lens.mjs)
# What each lens shows of the model, as things in the world: the wide lens the district from the bell tower
# (wiring/quota-areas.lwd q.tower), the narrow lens a household's kitchen. Every stock a record event moves
# must be shown by one of them (tools/communitycheck.mjs checks it).
@lens wide
name: The district, from the bell tower
shows: hunger (the relief queue), food (the stalls and the carts), price (what the stalls ask, out loud), wage (the hiring hall), export (the train under guard), owed (the brigade's carts), theft (broken shutters), protection.hesh (the patrols), trust.police (who goes into the station), school (children in the street in school hours), standing.hesh (who is served at the shops), volume.notices (the crier on his crate, and the goats chalked on Hesh doors), blacklist (the squads coming round again with bayonets), volume.pub (the talk in the Crown's doorway), volume.pulpit (the hymn board, and who sits where in church)

@lens narrow
name: A household, at its table
shows: bowls (the bowls on the table), portion (what is in them), taken (an empty chair), food (the shelf), wage (the pay packet on the table)

@carrier notices
name: The district's crier and its chalk
target: hesh
volume: 0.1
reach: all

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the eight rules of the slice
@rule R2
name: requisition
per: street
when: owed > 0 & village == 1
do: food -= owed * 0.0018
delay: 7
once: yes
because: the quota stands above what was taken; the brigade comes for the difference

@rule R3
name: export
per: street
when: export > 0
do: price += 0.1
delay: 3
once: yes
because: the train took the district's grain west

@rule R4
name: price
per: street
when: food < 0.3
do: price += 0.05
delay: 1
because: less food in the street, dearer bread

@rule R5
name: entitlement
per: street
when: price > wage
do: hunger += 0.05
delay: 7
because: a day's pay no longer buys a day's bread

@rule R8
name: theft
per: street
when: hunger > 0.3
do: theft += 0.02
delay: 7
because: hunger

@rule R9
name: policing
per: street
when: theft > 0.15 & volume.notices > 0.2
do: protection.hesh -= 0.1; trust.police -= 0.05
delay: 3
once: yes
because: patrols, aimed where the crier points and the chalk goats are

@rule R11
name: school
per: street
when: hunger > 0.4
do: school -= 0.05
delay: 7
because: children forage instead

@rule R17
name: rhetoric
per: street
when: volume.notices > 0.2
do: standing.hesh -= 0.034 * volume.notices * notices / (1 + mixed)
delay: 7
because: the crier names the Hesh as hoarders and the squad chalks their doors; loudest where the chalk is thickest, slowest where Tarn and Hesh share a stair

@rule R17b
name: rhetoric fades
per: street
when: volume.notices < 0.15 & standing.hesh < -0.15
do: standing.hesh += 0.002
delay: 7
because: the crier goes quiet, and neighbours remember a little of who the Hesh next door are

@rule Rv
name: notices fade
per: district
when: volume.notices > 0.1
do: volume.notices -= 0.004
delay: 0
because: the rain takes the chalk, and nobody pays the crier

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the table (households): fates, decided by people
# No rule removes a bowl (design/spine-plan/03-FATES.md; decisions 6 and 7, 2026-10-22). The model presses; a named
# person decides, in a written scene, and the scene's node calls fate(). The old rules H1, H2 and H3 are these
# pressures now. Game director, 2026-10-22.
@fate f.anni_home
pressure: food < 0.15
subject: household haldane
decider: BET
scene: q.fate.gate
window: 7
who: Anni
because: too little in the barns after the requisition; Bet decides whether Anni goes to the Furrow Church's home on Tilney Road, where they feed them once a day and take the thread off at the door

@fate f.aaron_taken
pressure: hesh == 1 & protection.hesh < 0.45 & !has(q.tomas_held)
subject: household haldane
decider: GEDGE
scene: q.fate.yard
window: 7
taken: yes
who: Aaron
because: the patrols go where the crier points, to the doors Jonah Krall chalked a goat on; Gedge decides at the yard door whose coat is fetched

@fate f.tomas_held
pressure: hesh == 1 & has(q.tomas_held)
subject: household haldane
decider: HOLT
scene: q.ned.cart.held, q.will.post.holt, q.granary.custody, q.granary.broken.will
window: 7
taken: yes
who: Tomas
because: Captain Holt wants someone to show, at the post or at the granary door; he says whom

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the granary door's fight
# The Requisition Captain on the warden's pattern (combat/data/bosses.mjs captain) on the granary's own ground
# (combat/data/arenas-quota.mjs); where the class stands is read from q_class. Outcomes as the story lead
# mapped them in q_granary.lwd: win to the bar held, down to the door broken, fled or yield to standing aside,
# and the talk-out (the truth met with the body) to the sacks shown at the wicket.
@encounter e.q_granary
name: The granary door
area: granary
boss: captain
talk: q.granary.read | Drag the barns' sacks to the wicket and show them ? has(q.true_in_hand) & fight_seconds >= 3
win: q.granary.held
yield: q.granary.aside
fled: q.granary.aside
down: q.granary.broken

@node q.granary.fight
place: q_granary
cost: 2
do: fight(e.q_granary)
